ngs":[{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Justify the new sidecar_transactions.py against existing in-repo prior art (_store/hlc.py::_hlc_lock, _commands/recent_creates.py::_journal_lock, _store/fsutil.atomic_write, alert_store.py flock usage) — either reuse/generalize them or correct the 'no existing lock-protected read-merge-write boundary to reuse' claim and state why a distinct module is needed.","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.0778,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan Context: 'there is no existing lock-protected read-merge-write boundary to reuse'","src/rebar/_store/hlc.py:102-118 — _hlc_lock: sibling '.rebar/hlc.lock', fcntl.flock(LOCK_EX) across one RMW","src/rebar/_commands/recent_creates.py:17-22,60-75 — _journal_lock documented as 'the _hlc_lock pattern', exclusive flock across read-prune-probe-append-rewrite as ONE critical section, atomic replace, malformed-JSON fail-open","src/rebar/_store/fsutil.py:85-121 — shared atomic_write (temp-in-same-dir + os.replace) already exists for the publication leg","src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/alert_store.py:54-62,87-107 — reconciler package already uses fcntl.flock and fsutil.atomic_write"],"finding":"The plan introduces a new sidecar_transactions.py 'stable-lock, delta-merge, atomic-publish owner' and asserts 'there is no existing lock-protected read-merge-write boundary to reuse', but the repository already implements this exact pattern in _store/hlc.py (_hlc_lock: dedicated sibling .lock + fcntl.flock(LOCK_EX) held across a read-modify-write) and _commands/recent_creates.py (_journal_lock, explicitly documented as reusing the _hlc_lock pattern, holding an exclusive flock across the whole read-prune-append-rewrite critical section with atomic replace and malformed-JSON fail-open). The publish leg it describes is already provided by _store/fsutil.atomic_write (same-dir temp + os.replace + fsync), and the same reconciler package already uses fcntl.flock in alert_store.py. The plan does not consider this prior art or justify a fresh module over reusing/generalizing the existing helpers.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc10bdcf43f410fff","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Context / Problem ('there is no existing lock-protected read-merge-write boundary to reuse') and Approach ('Add a focused shared sidecar_transactions.py owner')","norm_id":"n8fcf15385b7431e7","priority":0.7778,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Reviewer/maintainer evaluating whether a new shared 'transaction owner' is warranted vs. reusing hlc/recent_creates lock helpers","Future divergence between three parallel flock+atomic-write implementations of the same contract"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Cite _hlc_lock/_journal_lock as the established sibling-lock RMW pattern and fsutil.atomic_write as the atomic-publish primitive; state whether sidecar_transactions.py generalizes those helpers (preferred) or, if a separate owner is truly required (e.g. delta-merge semantics not present in the existing helpers), justify the distinction explicitly and drop the contradicted 'nothing to reuse' assertion.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"high","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State that the atomic-replace/durability leg of sidecar_transactions.py delegates to fsutil.atomic_write(fsync=True) rather than a new hand-rolled mkstemp+os.replace, matching the seam alert_store.py already adopted.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.2833,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["src/rebar/_store/fsutil.py:1 documents fsutil.atomic_write as the single consolidation point for temp-in-same-dir + os.replace, with fsync=True fsyncing file + dir for power-loss durability","src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/alert_store.py:107 already routes its sidecar rewrite through fsutil.atomic_write(permissions=..., fsync=True) and its docstring calls out that the prior hand-rolled mkstemp+os.replace lost durability guarantees","Current writers hand-roll mkstemp+os.replace with NO fsync: peer_confirmations.py:199-206, impossible_links.py:383-390, pass_io.py:217-221","Plan says 'durable atomic replace' but never names fsutil.atomic_write as the leg it reuses"],"finding":"The plan's 'durable atomic replace' leg risks re-hand-rolling temp+replace rather than reusing the existing fsutil.atomic_write(fsync=True) consolidation seam, which already owns the crash-atomic + fsync-durability contract and was already adopted by the sibling alert_store.py.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f88d745249517db3d","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach ('durable atomic replace'); Scope (sidecar_transactions.py)","norm_id":"n85c70717d88abcde","priority":0.6667,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A crash/OOM after os.replace but before dir fsync loses the just-published sidecar, contradicting the AC8 durability claim, if the new module re-implements the replace without fsync"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"In Approach, name fsutil.atomic_write(fsync=True) as the publication primitive the transaction owner wraps, so the new module contributes only the stable-lock read-merge boundary and not a duplicate temp+replace implementation.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.6667,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the disposition for flock-acquisition and atomic-write/replace failures (e.g. warn + fail-open, consistent with the malformed-file path) so all new I/O failure points fail safely.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.5312,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Only 'A malformed or non-object JSON sidecar' failure is covered with warn/fail-open","Absence: no stated behavior for lock-acquisition failure or a failed atomic replace during the transaction"],"finding":"The plan specifies error handling only for the malformed/non-object JSON case, but does not state the disposition when flock acquisition or the atomic temp-write/os.replace itself fails (I/O error, EINTR, disk full).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fbee8897c0f5383fa","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach (malformed-state handling) / Testing","norm_id":"n53d1bb0a350e898d","priority":0.4188,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["flock returns an error or the write/replace fails mid-transaction under disk pressure"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Extend the fail-open policy: on any lock-acquire or replace failure, emit a warning identifying the sidecar and skip persistence for that pass without raising, mirroring the malformed-file disposition.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State that the load-time baseline is captured as an INDEPENDENT deep snapshot (not an alias of the live records dict), since the stores mutate their records in place during the pass, so the save-time delta is computed against the truly-loaded state.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1812,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["impossible_links.py:357 assigns self._records[key] = {...} (in-place upsert) and :321 `del self._records[record_key(...)]` (in-place delete) during the pass","peer_confirmations.py:184 `self._records[key] = candidate` mutates in place","Plan text says 'capture the records loaded at construction as a baseline' without specifying it must be an independent copy immune to in-place mutation"],"finding":"The delta-merge mechanism requires the load-time baseline to be an independent snapshot, but the plan does not state this; the live record stores mutate their records dict IN PLACE (impossible_links.record() upserts into self._records; should_skip() does `del self._records[key]`), so a baseline captured as a reference to the live dict would be mutated alongside it and yield an empty/incorrect delta.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb15cbba00f1271f4","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach paragraph: 'capture the records loaded at construction as a baseline and calculate an explicit delta at save time'","norm_id":"n39a94c70fa3ae58f","priority":0.4188,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A pass records a new impossible link then saves: if the baseline aliases self._records, the delta sees no upsert and the new record is lost after merge","A pass deletes a record via should_skip then saves: an aliased baseline already reflects the deletion, so the delta computes no deletion and the record is resurrected on reload-merge"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"In the Approach, specify the baseline is a deep copy of the records taken at construction/load, decoupled from the live self._records mutated during the pass, so the delta (upserts + deletions) reflects only this pass's changes.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["4 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the lifecycle disposition of the stable sibling lock files: whether they are intentionally persistent (documented as such) or cleaned up, so they do not silently accumulate.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'creates a stable sibling lock file for each target and holds an exclusive fcntl.flock on that lock file'","Lifecycle covers create/update/consume but the plan is silent on whether the sibling lock files are ever removed or are intentionally persistent."],"finding":"The plan creates a stable sibling lock file per sidecar target but never specifies a RETIRE/cleanup path for those lock files, so they may accumulate indefinitely alongside sidecars.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"faf57d75a92a0c4fa","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'It creates a stable sibling lock file for each target'","norm_id":"n8185fac3751b6e57","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add a line clarifying that sibling lock files are deliberately long-lived (co-located with the sidecar, reused across passes) OR describe a cleanup path; if persistent, note this is intentional to preserve stable-inode locking.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Capture the stable-sibling-lock + delta-merge rationale (why the lock is on the sibling, not the JSON file) in an ADR or module docstring so the non-obvious inode/os.replace constraint survives future edits.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["T5e"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["New file 'src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/sidecar_transactions.py (new stable-lock, delta-merge, atomic-publish owner)'","Approach explains the non-obvious rationale ('lock deliberately not taken on the JSON file itself: os.replace changes that file's inode') — exactly the kind of decision that belongs in a durable doc","No documentation deliverable appears in Scope or Acceptance Criteria"],"finding":"The plan introduces a new shared cross-component owner (sidecar_transactions.py) establishing a novel stable-sibling-lock + delta-merge pattern consumed by three writers, but no ADR/AGENTS.md/design-doc capture of this architectural decision is planned.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f81974c9e6e88e2e3","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope / Approach","norm_id":"n870fda077c013012","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future maintainer sees a sibling lock file and 'fixes' it by locking the JSON file directly, reintroducing the inode/serialization bug"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add a module-level docstring in sidecar_transactions.py (or a short ADR) documenting the flock-on-sibling-file invariant and the delta-merge conflict semantics.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8571,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable